From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 01:13:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [peripherals] Keep the USB monitor across filtered events

CPeripheralBusUSB::WaitForUpdate() takes a NULL from
udev_monitor_receive_device() for a failed monitor and stops the bus
thread through Clear(). A monitor also returns NULL, with errno EAGAIN,
when none of the queued messages that woke poll() passes its filter.
systemd's libudev filters mostly in the kernel, but libudev-zero filters
only in userspace, so there the first event of another subsystem, such
as the input device of a USB keyboard being plugged in, ends USB
peripheral detection until Kodi restarts. Read messages until the
monitor returns NULL, as CALSADeviceMonitor does, and rescan if any of
them passed the filter.

Fixes: 098bec411b6d ("PeripheralBusUSBLibUdev: Filter on USB only")
Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
---
 .../peripherals/PeripheralBusUSBLibUdev.cpp     | 17 +++++++----------
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

--- a/xbmc/platform/linux/peripherals/PeripheralBusUSBLibUdev.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/platform/linux/peripherals/PeripheralBusUSBLibUdev.cpp
@@ -240,17 +240,14 @@ bool CPeripheralBusUSB::WaitForUpdate()
   if (m_bStop)
     return false;
 
-  /* we have to read the message from the queue, even though we're not actually using it */
-  struct udev_device *dev = udev_monitor_receive_device(m_udevMon);
-  if (dev)
-    udev_device_unref(dev);
-  else
+  /* the monitor returns NULL once no queued message passes its filter */
+  bool updated = false;
+  struct udev_device* dev;
+  while ((dev = udev_monitor_receive_device(m_udevMon)) != nullptr)
   {
-    CLog::Log(LOGERROR, "{} - failed to get device from udev_monitor_receive_device()",
-              __FUNCTION__);
-    Clear();
-    return false;
+    udev_device_unref(dev);
+    updated = true;
   }
 
-  return true;
+  return updated;
 }
